// RESTORE: the `sqlerror="msg"` testfile assertion keyword, across six files
// WAS: a testfile line could read `expr = sqlerror="message"`, asserting that a `DB.query`
//      lambda failed to compile to SQL with that message.
// ANCHOR: every piece sat immediately beside its `error=` equivalent, which STAYS, so restoring
//      is a matter of adding a second case next to each `TEError` arm. The pieces:
//
//   backend/src/LibParser/Parser.fs, in parseTestExpected, two arms beside the `error` ones:
//     | TIdent "sqlerror", TEquals, TStringLit s -> (WT.TESqlError s, i + 3)
//     | TIdent "sqlerror", TStringLit s, _ -> (WT.TESqlError s, i + 2)
//   and its doc line read `an \`error="msg"\` / \`sqlerror="msg"\` marker`.
//
//   backend/src/LibParser/WrittenTypes.fs, a case on TestExpected:
//     | TESqlError of string
//
//   backend/src/LibParser/Validation.fs, folded into the TEError arm:
//     | WT.TEError _
//     | WT.TESqlError _ -> []
//
//   backend/src/LibParser/TestModule.fs, two DU cases and two lowering arms:
//     | WTExpectedSqlError of string
//     | PTExpectedSqlError of string
//     | WT.TESqlError msg -> WTExpectedSqlError(String.normalize msg)
//     | WTExpectedSqlError msg -> return PTExpected.PTExpectedSqlError msg
//
//   backend/src/Builtins/Builtins.Language/Libs/Parser.fs, two arms that are now TEError:
//     | WT.TESqlError _ -> [ expr t.actual ]
//     | WT.TESqlError _ -> [ t.actual ]
//
//   backend/tests/Tests/LibExecution.Tests.fs, the branch that ran the assertion, comparing
//   `LibExecution.RTQueryCompiler.errorTemplate + expectedSqlError` against the actual error.
//
